# Edgar, King of Figaro's Two-Headed Coin counts only its controller's own flips: "the first time you flip one or more coins
# each turn" (CR 705.3). Every die the script fixes is face 2, a lost flip. Turn 4: Bot2's Mana Crypt flip in its upkeep is
# lost (3 damage), and Bot1's The Gold Saucer flip later that turn is still the first coin Bot1 flips, so Bot1 wins it
# whatever the coin shows and makes a Treasure.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
The Gold Saucer
Edgar, King of Figaro
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mana Crypt
Island x23

[Dice]
2; 2; 2; 2; 2

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.The Gold Saucer.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.The Gold Saucer.Activate(Ability: #1)
Bot1.Hand.Edgar, King of Figaro.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mana Crypt.Cast
Bot2.Pass

[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Life = 17
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 4
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.The Gold Saucer.Activate(Ability: #2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Token = true
